invariant: INV-16
file: hash_hw.h
catches: test/hash-builds.sh
reason: hash_hw.h no longer renames sha384_final on arm64, so the copies
  hkdf_hw.c and keysched_hw.c hold start each SHA-384 hash on the SHA-512
  instructions and end it on sha512.c. Every digest is the same, because
  the two paths keep one state, so no vector fails; a session that stated
  the instructions runs part of its SHA-384 calls on the portable code.
  The script reads the symbols each copy calls, for arm64 under the
  pinned clang, and requires the three SHA-384 calls on their _hw names
  and none on sha512.c's.

--- old
#define sha384_final sha384_final_hw
--- new
